{{!

    @template theme_ospira/login-aside

    Brand panel shown beside the login card on every pagelayout "login"
    page (log in, sign up, lost password) - see
    classes/output/core_renderer.php::standard_top_of_body_html().

    Injected at the top of the body rather than by overriding
    core/loginform, so none of Moodle's authentication markup (login
    token, identity providers, guest access, error banners) is forked
    into this theme. CSS puts it in the left column; see the
    .ospira-login-aside rules in scss/ospira.scss.

    The brand mark is drawn in CSS (@mixin ospira-brand-mark), not from
    pix/brand/logo-horizontal.png - that file is a dark wordmark on an
    opaque light pill, which reads as a grey chip on this gradient.

    The study scene below it is a CSS illustration - a laptop and a stack
    of books - wrapped around the one real photograph the theme ships. The photo is a
    cutout on a white background, which is exactly why it sits inside the
    laptop's white screen: it blends into it instead of showing as a white
    rectangle. The scene is aria-hidden - it is decoration, and it
    duplicates nothing the form needs.

    It carries no captions or counts. Nobody is logged in on this page, so
    a "module complete" or "certificate earned" chip would be invented -
    wrong for the first-time visitors this screen greets most.

    The headline is a <p>, not a heading: this panel precedes the login
    form's own <h1>, and an <h2> ahead of it would put the page's
    headings out of order for screen readers.

    Context variables required for this template - see
    theme_ospira_get_login_aside_context() in lib.php.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "homeurl": "https://learning.ospirax.com/?redirect=0",
        "photourl": "https://learning.ospirax.com/theme/image.php/ospira/theme_ospira/1/dashboard/family"
    }
}}
<aside class="ospira-login-aside">
    <div class="ospira-login-aside__decor" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="ospira-login-aside__orb ospira-login-aside__orb--one"></span>
        <span class="ospira-login-aside__orb ospira-login-aside__orb--two"></span>
        <span class="ospira-login-aside__dots"></span>
    </div>

    <div class="ospira-login-aside__inner">
        <a class="ospira-login-aside__brand" href="{{homeurl}}">
            <span class="ospira-login-aside__mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="ospira-login-aside__wordmark">ospira</span>
        </a>

        <p class="ospira-login-aside__headline">
            Learning that grows <span class="ospira-login-aside__headline-accent">with your child</span>
        </p>
        <p class="ospira-login-aside__lead">
            Parent-first courses for every stage of raising a child - practical,
            bite-sized, and built around your family.
        </p>

        <ul class="ospira-login-aside__ages">
            <li>Ages 1-5</li>
            <li>6-10</li>
            <li>11-15</li>
            <li>16-20</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="ospira-login-scene" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="ospira-login-scene__laptop">
                <div class="ospira-login-scene__screen">
                    <div class="ospira-login-scene__screen-inner">
                        <img class="ospira-login-scene__photo" src="{{photourl}}" alt="">
                        <div class="ospira-login-scene__screen-body">
                            <span class="ospira-login-scene__screen-title"></span>
                            <span class="ospira-login-scene__screen-bar"><span></span></span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ospira-login-scene__base"></div>
            </div>

            <div class="ospira-login-scene__books">
                <span class="ospira-login-scene__book ospira-login-scene__book--one"></span>
                <span class="ospira-login-scene__book ospira-login-scene__book--two"></span>
                <span class="ospira-login-scene__book ospira-login-scene__book--three"></span>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</aside>
